## 4. How Kafka Works in MaritimeIQ

### Publishing Events (Producer)

```csharp
// MaritimeIQ KafkaProducerService
public class KafkaProducerService
{
    private readonly IProducer<string, string> _producer;
    
    // Configuration for exactly-once semantics
    var producerConfig = new ProducerConfig
    {
        BootstrapServers = "kafka:9092",
        Acks = Acks.All,                    // Wait for all replicas
        EnableIdempotence = true,            // Exactly-once semantics
        CompressionType = CompressionType.Snappy,  // 30-40% compression
        BatchSize = 32768,                   // 32KB batches
        LingerMs = 10                        // Batch delay
    };
    
    public async Task PublishAISDataAsync(AISVesselData aisData)
    {
        var message = new Message<string, string>
        {
            Key = aisData.MMSI,              // Partition by MMSI
            Value = JsonSerializer.Serialize(aisData),
            Headers = new Headers
            {
                { "event-type", Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes("ais-position") },
                { "timestamp", Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(DateTime.UtcNow.ToString()) }
            }
        };
        
        await _producer.ProduceAsync("maritime.ais.data", message);
    }
}
```

**Key Features**:
- **Idempotent Producer**: `EnableIdempotence = true` ensures exactly-once delivery
- **Acks = All**: Wait for all replicas to acknowledge
- **Partitioning by Key**: MMSI ensures all messages from same vessel go to same partition
- **Compression**: Snappy compression reduces bandwidth by 30-40%
- **Batching**: 32KB batches for efficiency

### Consuming Events (Consumer)

```csharp
// MaritimeIQ KafkaConsumerService
public class KafkaConsumerService : BackgroundService
{
    private readonly IConsumer<string, string> _consumer;
    
    // Configuration for exactly-once processing
    var consumerConfig = new ConsumerConfig
    {
        BootstrapServers = "kafka:9092",
        GroupId = "maritime-processors",      // Consumer group
        EnableAutoCommit = false,             // Manual offset management
        EnableAutoOffsetStore = false,        // Manual offset storage
        AutoOffsetReset = AutoOffsetReset.Earliest
    };
    
    protected override async Task ExecuteAsync(CancellationToken stoppingToken)
    {
        // Subscribe to multiple topics
        _consumer.Subscribe(new[] 
        { 
            "maritime.ais.data",
            "maritime.environmental.sensors",
            "maritime.alerts",
            "maritime.voyage.events"
        });
        
        while (!stoppingToken.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            var consumeResult = _consumer.Consume(stoppingToken);
            
            try
            {
                // Process message
                await ProcessMessageAsync(consumeResult, stoppingToken);
                
                // Manual commit for exactly-once processing
                _consumer.Commit(consumeResult);
                _consumer.StoreOffset(consumeResult);
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                // Send to dead letter queue
                await SendToDeadLetterQueueAsync(consumeResult, ex);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

**Key Features**:
- **Manual Offset Management**: `EnableAutoCommit = false` for exactly-once processing
- **Consumer Groups**: Load balancing across multiple consumers
- **Multi-Topic Subscription**: Subscribe to multiple topics
- **Dead Letter Queue**: Failed messages sent to DLQ for investigation
- **Error Handling**: Comprehensive error handling with retry logic

