## 9. Kafka vs Other Messaging Systems

### Kafka vs RabbitMQ

**Kafka**:
- High throughput (millions/sec)
- Long retention (days/weeks)
- Stream processing
- Log-based
- Partition-based ordering

**RabbitMQ**:
- Message routing
- Complex routing rules
- Lower latency
- Queue-based
- Message acknowledgment

**When to Use Kafka**:
- High throughput requirements
- Event streaming
- Long retention needed
- Stream processing

**When to Use RabbitMQ**:
- Complex routing
- Lower latency requirements
- Traditional message queuing
- Work queues

### Kafka vs Traditional Databases

**Kafka**:
- Streaming data
- High write throughput
- Event log
- Real-time processing
- Append-only

**Databases**:
- Structured queries
- ACID transactions
- Complex relationships
- Historical analysis
- Update/delete operations

**When to Use Kafka**:
- Event streaming
- Real-time processing
- Event sourcing
- Data pipelines

**When to Use Databases**:
- Structured queries
- Complex relationships
- ACID transactions
- Historical analysis

